lies\":\"Retrospectively justifies the full 2.5:1 LR I cut to 1.7:1. CQ2's China conjunct falls from 0.60 to ~0.38 and CQ2 falls from 27 to roughly 17-18. It also weakens the Chinese savings-glut leg of r*, adding 10-15bp to CQ4, and raises CQ3's China leg, lifting the CQ3 P50 by ~10bp and CQ6-A by ~2pp.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"GDP-weighted OECD-38 core CPI/PCE prints a trailing three-year average BELOW 2.0% while the US policy rate is cut below 2.5% nominal — the disinflationary-stagnation branch arriving early, most plausibly via the AI-Q4 capex impairment leaving excess datacenter and generation capacity as a deflationary power-price impulse.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies my front-loaded inflation object, which is the basis of both CQ2 and the CQ6 inflation cuts. CQ2 falls from 27 to roughly 14-16; CQ6-D rises from 15 to ~24 and CQ6-C falls from 22 to ~13; CQ4 P50 falls 30-40bp as both r* and the term premium ease into a demand shortfall; hypothesis plank (c) rises from 42 toward 60, since 'falls in the 2030s' would be vindicated.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run2 wave 2 bayes seat, effort 'rstar'."}}